  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the woman eating crackers as a metaphor for media bias",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the woman eating crackers, interpreting her action as a metaphor for the media's fixation on racialized violence. The meme implies that the user (as a viewer or critic) is aware of the media's oversimplification and is pointing out the 'forgotten' element ('the crackers'), thereby projecting their critical stance onto the visual subject. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the implied audience (the user) is positioned as the one who 'sees' the metaphor and understands the critique.",
